**Definition 9.4 (unresolved full common-instance problem).** Let $Q$ be
the original continuation/audit task with original terminal type/output
and admitted experiments, and $Q_{G_{\rm sel}}$ the task additionally
exposing the new history operations. Neither is raw-state equality,
history equality or actual current access. A claimed four-expression
solution on this same growing carrier must still define independently
natural spatial, temporal, boundary and retained/callable-memory views
$V_i$, and prove, for each separately on its stated common domain,

$$
V_i(x)=V_i(y)\Longrightarrow Q(x)=Q(y),\qquad
Q(x)=Q(y)\Longrightarrow V_i(x)=V_i(y).
$$

It must also prove simultaneous legality, label and successor transport,
and original terminal readouts, on all original and added raw/partial
phases, including mode acquisition, parser, bank, descriptor, code,
loan, copy and return cuts. Four copies of manifest/$I_k$/$k$ or an
intersection of kernels are not independent natural definitions. PVC's
serializers and paid cycle still need an actually initialized nonconflicting
ARC74 placement/owner/input/service/return bridge. Its unused verifier
and fixed-$H$ continuing comparison task do not transfer to this occupied
verifier and original terminal task. A serialized geometry is not a
physically materialized old graph, and a printed old token is not a live
old handle.

The recovery result covers exactly acquisition-or-later cuts in an actual
completed predecessor admitted at Ready. Its current uncompleted flight
becomes eligible only if it later returns. The original gate00 suffix has
no new history entry or later Ready; CAP Theorem 17.3/ARC Proposition 11.2
therefore retains its last-Ready horizon. CAP Proposition 17.4 excludes
the final cut for any completed strict-past service, without excluding
every proper preterminal cut. No posthalt operation is added. Any further
prehalt service must supply its own initialized entry, retained input,
authority, original-task correspondence and paid return. CAP Corollary
16.7's same-output/no-posthalt-audit terminal fibres also retain their
scoped force: full history cannot simply replace the original terminal
response. These supplied boundaries are not new impossibility results.

Generic-source progress and original-task acceptance retain Assumption
1.3 and ARC Definition 9.4. Theorem 7.2's one-source unbounded finite
growth and the general acquired-cut interface do not settle these
remaining four-view, converter, task-kernel, final-suffix or infinite-
continuation obligations.

